* Node: N1 (13th round; R486 before). Round type: falsification and novelty of a new criterion in a fresh outside record (Zenodo 24383660, A. Ursachi, 'Local Weil Positivity and Signed Prime-Deficit Criteria', 20 Nov 2026, CP8.26), plus three exploration scouts. The Friday 20 Nov arXiv listing was still missing at 04:25 UTC (math.NT/new: Thursday 19 Nov); it is the next round.
* Claims under test: Thm 5.2: RH ⟺ there is a finite C ≥ 0 with q[f] ≥ −C‖f‖₂² for every f ∈ C_c^∞(R; C) (5.3); proof: (5.3) extends to the weighted domain Y_η (5.2), η > 1/2, by continuity and density; Lemma 5.1: every translate K_a of the Riemann–Pólya kernel K (K̂ = Ξ) is q-null against Y_η and span{K_a} is dense in L²; so q[f] = q[f − r_n] ≥ −C‖f − r_n‖₂² → 0 and Weil's criterion gives RH. Thm 6.1: RH ⟺ W(X) ≥ −C eventually, W(X) = Σ_{n≥2} Λ(n)n^{−1/2}(log 2 − |log(n/X)|)_+ − (6√2 − 8)√X, by Landau's theorem; archived certificate W(X) > −0.06353666 for 4 ≤ X ≤ 262144.
